bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">ground coriander</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a hint of sweetness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">turmeric powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">offers vibrant color and health benefits</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1–2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">red chili powder or paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for that perfect spicy touch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garam masala</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">a blend of warming spices</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to bring all the flavors together</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">vegetable oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">helps distribute the spices evenly</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6332-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6332\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For whisking the ingredients together.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To ensure a smooth paste.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6332-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6332-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6332\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6332-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Whisk the Yogurt &#8211; In a bowl, whisk the yogurt until smooth. This will be the creamy base of your tandoori paste.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6332-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add Flavorful Ingredients &#8211; Add ginger-garlic paste, lemon juice, and oil; stir to combine. These ingredients will bring a zesty kick to your paste.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6332-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Mix in the Spices &#8211; Mix in cumin, coriander, turmeric, chili powder, garam masala, and salt. Each spice adds its unique character to the paste.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6332-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Stir Until Uniform &#8211; Stir well until a uniform paste forms. You want it to be smooth and well-blended.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6332-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Use or Store &#8211; Use immediately to marinate meat, seafood, or vegetables, or store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Enjoy the burst of flavors!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      \n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here are the ingredients you&#8217;ll need to whip up a delicious tandoori paste.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Colorful-Ingredients-for-Tandoori-Paste.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for tandoori paste including yogurt, spices, and lemon juice arranged on a wooden table.\" class=\"wp-image-6330\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Colorful-Ingredients-for-Tandoori-Paste.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Colorful-Ingredients-for-Tandoori-Paste-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 cup plain yogurt</strong> – provides a creamy base</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons ginger-garlic paste</strong> – adds depth and aroma</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon lemon juice</strong> – gives a zesty kick</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon ground </strong><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>cumin</strong> </a>– enhances flavor with earthy notes</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon ground </strong><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coriander\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>coriander</strong> </a>– adds a hint of sweetness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turmeric\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">turmeric </a>powder</strong> – offers vibrant color and health benefits</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1–2 tablespoons red chili powder or paprika</strong> – for that perfect spicy touch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garam_masala\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">garam masala</a></strong> – a blend of warming spices</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon salt</strong> – to bring all the flavors together</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon vegetable oil</strong> – helps distribute the spices evenly</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-tandoori-paste\"><strong>How to Make Tandoori Paste</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making tandoori paste is a delightful journey into the world of flavors. With just a few ingredients, you can create a vibrant marinade that will elevate your dishes. The preparation time is about 10 minutes, and while there&#8217;s no cooking time, allowing the paste to rest for at least 30 minutes enhances the flavors.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Making-Tandoori-Paste.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making tandoori paste with yogurt, spices, and lemon juice.\" class=\"wp-image-6331\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Making-Tandoori-Paste.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Making-Tandoori-Paste-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Whisk the Yogurt</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk the yogurt until smooth. This will be the creamy base of your paste.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Flavorful Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add ginger-garlic paste, lemon juice, and oil; stir to combine. These ingredients will bring a zesty kick to your paste.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Mix in the Spices</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Mix in cumin, coriander, turmeric, chili powder, garam masala, and salt. Each spice adds its unique character to the paste.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Stir Until Uniform</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir well until a uniform paste forms. You want it to be smooth and well-blended.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Use or Store</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Use immediately to marinate meat, seafood, or vegetables, or store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Enjoy the burst of flavors!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Condiment</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Indian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>30 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>40 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>As a marinade for meats, seafood, or vegetables</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-tandoori-paste\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making tandoori paste</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use fresh spices for a vibrant flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust the chili level to suit your taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the paste marinate for at least an hour for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try adding yogurt for a creamier texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store leftovers in an airtight container for up to a week.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-tandoori-paste\"><strong>How to Serve this tandoori paste</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Marinate chicken, tofu, or veggies for a zesty grill night.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Spread on naan or pita for a quick and tasty appetizer.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix into yogurt for a refreshing dip or sauce.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a flavorful base for curries or stews.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with basmati rice or quinoa for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top salads with a drizzle for an exotic twist.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and preserving your tandoori paste is simple and effective:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing tandoori paste Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to one week.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing tandoori paste</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Portion the paste into freezer-safe bags or containers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove excess air to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to three months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating tandoori paste</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat gently in a saucepan over low heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or oil if it’s too thick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir occasionally to maintain a smooth texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs-1\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">1. What is tandoori paste made of?</h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Tandoori paste is a vibrant blend of spices and ingredients that typically includes yogurt, garlic, ginger, cumin, coriander, turmeric, paprika, and garam masala. These ingredients come together to create a rich, flavorful paste that is perfect for marinating meats and vegetables before cooking them in a tandoor or oven.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">2. What is a substitute for tandoori paste?</h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>If you don&#8217;t have tandoori paste on hand, you can create a quick substitute by mixing yogurt with spices like cumin, coriander, paprika, turmeric, and a bit of lemon juice. This combination will give you a similar flavor profile, making it a great alternative for your recipes.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">3. Is tikka paste the same as tandoori paste?</h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While both tikka paste and tandoori paste share some common ingredients, they are not the same. Tikka paste is typically used for marinating smaller pieces of meat or vegetables, while tandoori paste is often used for whole pieces. The flavor profiles can also differ slightly, with tikka paste sometimes being creamier due to the addition of cream or coconut milk.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">4. What do you do with tandoori paste?</h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Tandoori paste is incredibly versatile! You can use it to marinate chicken, fish, or vegetables before grilling or baking. It can also be added to curries for an extra kick of flavor or used as a base for sauces. The possibilities are endless, so feel free to get creative in the kitchen!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have your homemade tandoori paste, get ready to embark on a flavorful journey! It’s so simple and rewarding to whip up this vibrant blend of spices. Whether you’re marinating chicken, veggies, or tofu, each bite will transport you to a cozy kitchen filled with warmth and laughter. Enjoy every delicious moment!</p>\n",
